dialect protocol
protocol stdio.jpg.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.jpg
start record

# P2-FG2: REAL binary op frame, replacing F6's `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary shortcut
# (`../../🦀️component.rs`'s old `OpBinary::encode_op` -- see that file's `#region OpCodecs` for the
# upgraded implementation). `format u8` (`store::OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `tag u8` (the
# `JpgMutation` variant's declaration-order ordinal, 0=`NoMutation` .. 11=`SetReEncodeQuality`,
# same order `print_jpg_mutation`'s own match arms use) as two REAL fixed fields, individually
# protocol-walked.
#
# Past that header, the variant's own payload (which may embed a full `JpgSnapshot` for
# `SetSnapshot`, or an id/index-keyed collection item) is one opaque trailing `bytes` chain rather
# than sixteen tag-conditional field lists: `Cond` can only guard on a field's WHOLE value against
# a literal (real here -- `tag`'s value genuinely selects the payload SHAPE), but `walk_protocol`
# has no per-tag-value BRANCHING construct for an ARM-shaped field list outside `repeat` (`repeat`
# itself is for a REPEATED tag-dispatched sequence, not a single one-shot tag-then-payload
# record) -- and `SetSnapshot`'s own payload independently hits the `protocol-array-of-records`
# mechanism gap (`📖️grammar-recipe.md` §5: quant/huffman-table/other-segment lists are
# heterogeneous-shaped repeated records, not one repeated scalar `Prim`). The Rust
# `encode_op`/`decode_op` side (`../../🦀️component.rs`'s `#region OpCodecs`/`§SnapshotBinaryCodec`)
# stays genuinely, fully structured (tag-dispatched, real varint/fixed-width fields, real
# collection counts, reusing `../🔺️diff/🦀️component.rs`'s own real binary value codecs) and
# round-trip tested independently -- this protocol file's opaque tail is a DESCRIPTION-layer
# boundary only, the same honest treatment `📰xml`'s own upgraded mutations protocol gives its
# recursive `XmlNode`/`XmlNodePath` payload.
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8
chain payload bytes
